71-## 3. Repository Layout
72-
73-```text
74-ai-automation/
75-├── .github/workflows/ai-automation.yml  # CI: Chrome + OpenCode + scheduled scan
76-├── data/                     # Authorized targets and target details
77-├── skills/                   # Agent and security testing skill files
78-│   ├── AGENT.md              # This file: binding instructions for the agent
79-│   ├── client-side-skill.md  # Client-side methodology (provided/approved)
80-│   └── server-side-skill.md  # Server-side methodology (provided/approved)
81-├── creds/                    # Authorized test credentials and account details
82-├── vulnebleti/               # Vulnerability notes, payloads, bypasses, references
83:├── result/                   # All outputs, evidence, findings, reports, logs
84-└── tools/                    # Reusable automation scripts and cmd.txt
85-```
86-
87-Directory contracts:
88-
89-- **`data/`** — Read-only during a run. May contain domain-only targets or URL
90-  lists. Treat every non-hidden, non-placeholder file as target information.
91-- **`skills/AGENT.md`** — This file. Read it completely at the start of every
92-  session. Always launch from the repository root so all relative paths resolve.
93-- **`skills/client-side-skill.md` and `skills/server-side-skill.md`** —
94-  Read-only during a run. Read the client-side skill first, then the
95-  server-side skill. Follow each skill exactly.
96-- **`creds/`** — Read-only during a run. Contains disposable test credentials
97-  (for example `test-account.txt`). Test-account credentials, cookies, and
98:  tokens may be copied into `result/`, logs, and reports. Never add real
99-  credentials.
100-- **`vulnebleti/`** — Read-only during a run. Use it for vulnerability classes,
101-  payloads, bypass techniques, and testing ideas. Do not treat notes as proof.
102-- **`result/`** — The only directory for run outputs. The CI workflow preserves
103-  it when `data/targets.txt` is unchanged and resets it only when the target
104:  input changes. Read `result/logs/target-state.txt`, prior inventory, findings,
105-  and logs first, and continue untested work. Write progress and evidence early
106-  and often.
107-- **`tools/`** — Reusable scripts. The agent may create or repair
108-  `tools/chrome-mcp-start.sh` on first use. Do not edit `tools/cmd.txt`; that
109-  file is user-owned and defines the launch command.
110-
111-Do not modify `data/`, `skills/`, `creds/`, or `vulnebleti/`. Do not write
112-outside the repository except under `/tmp` for browser profiles, logs, and
113-temporary PoC servers.
